# Security Rules

## Authentication

- Use Supabase Auth.
- Validate the current user on protected server operations.
- Do not trust user IDs supplied by the browser.
- Derive identity from the authenticated session.
- Protect workspace and document routes.

## Authorization

Document roles:
- Owner
- Editor
- Viewer

Permissions:
- Owner: full control.
- Editor: read and update document content.
- Viewer: read-only access.

Only the owner can:
- Rename documents.
- Share documents.
- Modify collaborator permissions.
- Remove collaborators.
- Delete documents.

## Database security

- Enable RLS on every user-data table.
- Write explicit SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE policies as applicable.
- Enforce ownership and membership checks in the database.
- Prevent unauthorized membership changes.
- Prevent owner_id manipulation.
- Prevent permission escalation.
- Avoid recursive RLS policy designs.
- Test access using multiple authenticated users.

Never rely on frontend checks as the security boundary.

## File validation

- Support .txt and .md only.
- Enforce a 2 MB maximum.
- Validate extension, MIME type and size.
- Reject unsupported and malformed files.
- Do not execute uploaded content.
- Escape or safely render imported content.

## Secrets

- Never expose the Supabase service-role key.
- Never commit .env.local.
- Provide .env.example with placeholder values.
- Keep privileged operations server-side.
